        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.186,
            0.617,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "How can we write 234 tenths in decimal form?"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.22,
            0.343,
            0.256
          ],
          "content": "234\\;{\\rm{tenths}} = \\frac{234}{10}",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.26,
            0.329,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{200}{10} + \\frac{30}{10} + \\frac{4}{10}",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.301,
            0.305,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&=20 + 3 + \\frac{4}{10} \\\\&= 23.4.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.369,
            0.843,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": "| Hundreds | Tens | Units | Tenths | Hundredths |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  | 234 |  |\n|  | 2 | 3 | 4 |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_table_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.471,
            0.846,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": "Write these quantities in decimal form: (a) 234 hundredths, (b) 105 tenths."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.528,
            0.514,
            0.552
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3.5 Units of Measurement"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.563,
            0.39,
            0.585
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Length Conversion"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.595,
            0.846,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "We have been using a scale to measure length for a few years. We already know that 1 cm = 10 mm (millimeters)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.641,
            0.394,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "How many cm is 1 mm?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.674,
            0.641,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "1 mm = 10 1 cm = 0.1 cm (i.e., one-tenth of a cm)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.721,
            0.54,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "How many cm is (a) 5 mm? (b) 12 mm?"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.753,
            0.41,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "5\\  mm =\\frac{5}{10}\\  cm =0.5\\  cm",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.793,
            0.418,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}12\\; mm  &= 10\\; mm  + 2\\; mm  \\\\&= 1\\; cm  + \\frac{2}{10}\\; cm  \\\\&= 1.2\\; cm .\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
